  "result": "I fixed the clamping bug: `IntRange(clamp=True)` with an open bound now returns a value inside the range. All 45 tests in `tests/test_types.py` ran: 43 passed and 2 were skipped.\n\nThe fix is one line in `src/click/types.py:754`: `return bound - dir` is now `return bound + dir`. The old code moved the clamped value outward instead of inward. For example, `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `-5` into `-1`; it now returns `1`. The open-max case now returns `4` for a max of 5, instead of `6`.\n\nI added these two examples as test cases in `tests/test_types.py`.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
